WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.329
Scenario: A browser extension promises to summarize every page.

2
00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:06.658
It requests permission to read and change all data

3
00:00:06.658 --> 00:00:09.986
on every website, including internal work portals. Safest response:

4
00:00:09.986 --> 00:00:13.315
Option C: Check organizational approval, publisher provenance, necessity and

5
00:00:13.315 --> 00:00:16.644
permission scope before installation. Broad access to every site

6
00:00:16.644 --> 00:00:19.973
creates significant data and account exposure and should be

7
00:00:19.973 --> 00:00:23.301
justified and approved. Option A is unsafe because Using

8
00:00:23.301 --> 00:00:26.630
another person’s profile does not resolve the extension’s access

9
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.959
or policy risks. Option B is unsafe because Private

10
00:00:29.959 --> 00:00:33.288
mode does not necessarily prevent an extension from accessing

11
00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:36.616
permitted page content. Option D is unsafe because Ratings

12
00:00:36.616 --> 00:00:40.315
do not establish the publisher’s trustworthiness or justify broad permissions.

13
00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:43.644
In practice: Do not install until the extension is

14
00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:47.342
approved and its permissions are proportionate to a documented need.

15
00:00:47.342 --> 00:00:50.671
Key takeaway: An extension with broad permissions can access

16
00:00:50.671 --> 00:00:54.000
sensitive page data; assess source and scope before use.
